<title>CHINA: China's Guangxi region sees sugar cane output up.</title>
<headline>China's Guangxi region sees sugar cane output up.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's largest sugar-producing region Guangxi is expected to produce more than 23 million tonnes of sugar cane in 1996, an increase of two million tonnes compared with 1995, the Xinhua news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>Local refineries are expected to produce 2.4 million tonnes of sugar, Xinhua said, quoting local officials.</p>
<p>Guangxi has been China's number one sugar cane-producing region for four consecutive years, the agency said. It refined 2.33 million tonnes of sugar in the 1995-96 refining season, accounting for 37.41 percent of the nationwide figure.</p>
<p>The 1996-97 refining season starts in November this year, Xinhua said. It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
